# Files the Vercel CLI must never upload with the source.
#
# Without this, `vercel deploy` ships the local .env into the build context.
# Next.js only falls back to .env files for variables NOT already present in
# the environment, so any variable you forget to configure in the Vercel
# dashboard silently picks up your LOCAL development value instead of failing
# loudly — which is how a placeholder phone number reached production.
#
# Production configuration must come from Vercel's environment variables only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build output and tooling — Vercel builds these itself.
.next
node_modules
.git

# Local-only scripts and test artefacts.
/private
*.log
